  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ea9744ac-351a-5e90-87ce-90429eaa6a13" activityNameId="744e9682-880d-50e1-b53a-ced95d2fc0a0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Well for exploration and production, onshore</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Well for exploration and production, onshore
Process for all types of onshore drilling operations.;
3262b4af-fed2-3190-876f-bf5edca24ffd
All materials and emissions for drilling of an offshore bore hole and finishing of the well.  Not including energy, venting and flaring which is covered in general production data.
Location:  Data for NG, IN and multinational companies.
Technology: Onshore drilling.
Time period: Time of publication in literature and environmental reports. Most data are valid for the end of the 90ties.
Production volume: About 30km in NG and 80km in India and 15km of a company in one year.
Sampling: Publication in environmental reports and other literature.
Extrapolations: Applied on all onshore drilling operations. There might be differences depending on type of geological formation.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3262b4af-fed2-3190-876f-bf5edca24ffd.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">GLO</shortname>
        <comment>
